{
  "meaning": "Starts of the ordinary pickup clocks in the game, each section one recording: `recorded` is the PR that recorded it, the commit that added it and the frozen engine head. `backed_up_start`: the normal underground entrance and exit started on fully backed-up belts with new empty machines and hands, under the fixed windows of their swings-1 clock, at offsets 0 and 1287. `cold_start`: 57 clocked cold starts from the harness's staged start, the game's own lane phase at placement (`frame_offset`: model held[i] is native sample i + 4). Each of its `clocks` is named by the first 12 hex of the hash it was recorded under, which included its text; `clock_sha256` is the sha256 of its identity (`clockIdentity`: the blueprint without its text or metadata, and the schedule), the clock the selection must still make (the generation test), and `recorded_clock_sha256` the one the runs were recorded on (the game test); a unit test requires them equal, so a clock that moved is recorded again before `recorded_clock_sha256` changes.",
